WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:04.680
When it comes to popcorn movies, the phrase
"dumb fun" might get used by fans.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.140
And a lot of people found Suicide Squad to
be just that: dumb fun!

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.130
But...was there just a bit too much dumb?

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:16.560
With a collection A-list actors as ridiculous
comic bad guys, you'd think it'd be hard to

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.580
get it wrong, and while the end result has
some great moments, the final cut that made

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.380
it to the silver screen was reportedly wrecked
by the studio making cuts.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.560
While you may have seen the extended edition
at home, here are some dumb things in the

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.140
theatrical version of Suicide Squad that everyone
just ignored.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:34.640
The magic machine

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.270
Enchantress exists so the Suicide Squad can
go up against a sexy villain with a generic

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.270
plan.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:42.320
"Uh, please don't touch me.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.390
Please don't touch me."

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:45.370
Her big evil idea?

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:50.000
Build a mysterious "machine" to end mankind…
and that's pretty much it.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.641
The device, apparently powered by Enchantress'
sweet dance moves and makeout sessions, is

00:00:54.641 --> 00:00:56.390
never actually explained.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:00.870
She just says she's going to create a giant
garbage tornado to get back at humanity, then

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.280
it opens up a hole in the sky.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.030
Enchantress can transform any human into a
member of her jelly army, and her brother

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:10.189
has crazy fire-whips for arms that can slice
through anything.

00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:14.630
If you can't take over the world with just
that, you're doing it wrong, lady.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:15.700
Justice League who?

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.509
By the time Suicide Squad rolled around, The
Flash and Wonder Woman were already introduced

00:01:20.509 --> 00:01:21.649
to movie audiences.

00:01:21.649 --> 00:01:27.469
To have them disappear during one of the biggest
metahuman crises the world has ever seen doesn’t

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:28.469
quite add up.

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:31.929
It would have been simpler to set the film
pre-Man of Steel than to pretend that these

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:35.479
heroes didn't exist for the big fight of Suicide
Squad.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:40.470
We could accept if Batman called in sick after
learning his lesson about not fighting superpowered

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.630
villains…

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.300
"Oh —-"

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.220
...but no Wonder Woman?

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:47.359
She's all about this kind of stuff.

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:48.899
The helicopter crash

00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:52.999
Suspension of disbelief is pretty critical
when viewing any superhero film, but that

00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:56.759
doesn't mean you have to toss out everything
you know about physics and biology in the

00:01:56.759 --> 00:01:58.719
name of action packed evil shenanigans.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:00.220
"Evil shenanigans."

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:04.280
When the Suicide Squad's helicopter is shot
down as they're entering the city, and does

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.920
about a dozen flips on the ground, you'd expect
a broken fingernail, at the very least.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:13.630
The super-tough Killer Croc might come out
okay, but somehow, everyone hops out of the

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.870
downed 'copter like they're fresh out of the
shower.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.470
"What a ride!"

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:21.580
We know they're bad guys, mostly because Harley
Quinn announces it frequently —

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.910
"We're bad guys, it's what we do."

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.000
— and we know they're tough.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.120
But there's no way that someone didn't at
least bang a knee in that crash.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:38.900
"Aaahhhh, aaahhhhh"

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.360
Look we'll say it again: we're calling shenanigans.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.170
"I swear to God I'll pistol whip the next
guy that says shenanigans!"

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.510
"Hey Farva, what's the name of that restaurant
you like with all the goofy —- on the walls

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:53.040
and the mozzarella sticks?"

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:53.780
"You mean Shenanigans?"

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.280
"Ohhhh!"

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.090
The only bomb in the universe

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.550
The first attempt at blowing up Incubus failed
because Enchantress cut out on the team moments

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:06.900
before the bad-guy-destroying bomb went off,
with no way to reset the countdown.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:12.000
Instead of setting the bomb for five minutes
or something, they base an entire plan around

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.510
an unreliable magical weirdo.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.060
"Needless to say the whole thing was a bad
idea."

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:21.410
Even stranger, they only have one of these
bombs, and somehow can’t make another, so

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:24.280
they have to retrieve it from a flooded subway
system.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:30.600
At the very least, this makes Killer Croc's
swimming, uh, "powers" actually relevant,

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.310
but it's never explained why this one bomb
is the only bomb.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:37.880
Or why wiping out the building from above
isn't an option.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.620
Or why don't they just use a drone or something?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.160
Why must the Squad do everything the hard
way?

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.820
"We're bad guys, it's what we do."

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:46.820
Oh.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:48.700
Okay, then.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.560
Terrible admissions policy

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:55.520
Amanda Waller's entire reason for assembling
the Suicide Squad was so she could have her

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.340
own group of super-people she could control.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.600
But the team leaves a lot to be desired.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.320
While it’s kinda accurate to the comics,
the film doesn’t really make the reasons

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.150
for their roster clear.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:10.940
Villains like Killer Croc, Diablo, and Deadshot
make sense to have around, because their skills

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:12.260
can be pretty handy.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.950
But what about Harley Quinn and Captain Boomerang?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:18.979
Harley Quinn has been shown to be a clever
tactician in the comics, but all of that's

00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:22.139
replaced with tight shorts in the film.

00:04:22.139 --> 00:04:25.069
Last time we checked, hotpants weren’t a
superpower.

00:04:25.069 --> 00:04:30.310
Captain Boomerang is a sociopathic bank robber
who can throw boomerangs, which are the least

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.539
effective weapon of all time.

00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:34.490
While we're on the subject of the Captain...

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:36.330
Boomerang returns

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:40.879
After the team has its near-breakup toward
the middle of the film, the gang decides to

00:04:40.879 --> 00:04:44.570
get back together and go face off against
Enchantress.

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:48.659
It's fairly well established why everyone
decides to stick around for the big fight,

00:04:48.659 --> 00:04:52.880
but then Boomerang just randomly jumps in
with them as they do their heroic walk off

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.110
into battle.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.820
Unlike most of the other team members, Boomerang
never really showed any interest in being

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:00.400
a team player.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.150
So why does he come back?

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.509
Is it because, uh, he's all into boomerangs?

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:07.090
And they always come back?

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.540
"Oh no, it's coming back this way!"

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.910
"That throwing stick stunt of yours has boomeranged
on us!"

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.249
And where does he keep getting those beers?

00:05:18.249 --> 00:05:20.939
Maybe that’s his real superpower.

00:05:20.939 --> 00:05:23.520
"Somethin' wrong Yank?"

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:27.110
"No, it's pretty big, I guess."

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:28.180
Thanks for watching!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.819
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:30.819 --> 00:05:32.990
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

